  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 8.1. Increased capacity of member States to develop new or reformed sustainable national social protection strategies, policies or legal frameworks to extend coverage and enhance benefit adequacy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In September 2020, as a result of consultations with different stakeholders of Somalia, such as the Ministry of Labour &amp; Social Affairs (MOLSA), the Ministry of Finance and the Ministry of Planning, as well as with the Federation of Somali Trade Unions (FESTU), the Somali Chambers Commerce and Industry (SCCI) and development partners including WFP and UNICEF, the Federal Government of Somalia, through the MOLSA, approved and launched the implementation framework of social protection policy. The implementation framework is aligned with SDG targets set by the Federal Government and aligned with R202 &amp; C102.  The Framework will put into practice the implementation of the social protection policy launched in March 2019.  Overall, it will support the federal government towards coming up with comprehensive social protection programmes that benefits all vulnerable Somali populations. With the support of UNSDG fund, ILO has trained 17 (11 male, 6 female ) participants coming from the Federal Government, the Ministry of Labour &amp; Social Affair (MOLSA) and UN partners on overall social protection so as they can support the national consultant who will be   collecting and monitoring social protection data in Somalia. The participants were also trained on the  practical use of the Social Security Inquiry tool (SSI), where they were provided of an After the training, the ILO has completed the data collection exercise using the Social Security Inquiry (SSI) tool. The data was reviewed by ILO to guarantee quality control. In June 2021, ILO presented the results to different stakeholders such as UN, INGO, other line ministries and donors such as EU, Italy, WB during the Government Development Partner Working Group (GWDG) that was organized by MOLSA. The importance of Social Security Inquiry (SSI) towards monitoring the progress on social protection coverage and as well as to report to SDG 1.3 was underpinned.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">8.1.1. Number of member States with new or revised national social protection policies to extend coverage, enhance comprehensiveness and/or increase adequacy of benefits</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
